--     ruling-basket census): two ruled model corrections, plus a
--     correction to the "activity" band-wide note immediately above
--     (which named `A_engine` as a leaf gaining `activity sustained` --
--     no longer accurate now that `A_engine` is a composite, see item 1
--     below; preserved above verbatim per this file's own "supersede,
--     don't delete" convention, corrected here).
--
--     (1) THREE-VOCABULARY ENGINE-STATUS DECOMPOSITION (ledger row 2073,
--     commissioner ADR-0008 ruling): "the engine status line is a
--     MISCATEGORIZATION as one unit ('metric band'); the compliant
--     decomposition is three vocabularies: {winrate, lead} | {pps,
--     latency, watchdog} | {queue}... three distinct leaves/groups with
--     their own demand bases, activity states, and candidate homes --
--     not one strip that must fit somewhere." Before this stage,
--     `A_engine[go, action+info]` was exactly that one strip -- a single
--     leaf conflating the connect/disconnect + engine-controls ACTION
--     cluster with all six INFO readouts (winrate, scoreLead, pps,
--     latency, watchdog, queue) in one `action+info` facet bag, the
--     "one unit" framing the ruling names as the miscategorization (this
--     file never used the literal string "metric band", but the
--     single-leaf shape it corrects IS that framing under a different
--     name -- corrected here regardless of the exact prior wording).
--
--     Re-encoded as `H(A_engine_controls, A_engine_eval, A_engine_health,
--     A_engine_queue)`, replacing the bare leaf in the SAME tree
--     position (still one child of the side column's own `V(...)`) --
--     no `[TAG]` bracket, since that annotation is Exclusive(`T`)-only
--     per the grammar (SPEC.md §1.1), not available on an `H`/`V` split.
--     The wrapping `H(...)`'s own sizing block carries
--     the SAME `{60px, envelope: {disconnected, connected}}` height
--     reservation the single leaf declared before -- this stage does not
--     touch the cluster's own overall standing height, only its
--     INTERIOR structure. Its own NEW `gap 4px` (between the four
--     vocabulary leaves) matches this file's own established
--     `--space-tight` tier -- the SAME gap every other tight row in this
--     file already uses (this row's own siblings, the outer side
--     column's own `V(...)`, and the tree/panels row all declare the
--     identical `gap 4px, --space-tight`). Four leaves, one per vocabulary plus the
--     action cluster the ruling's own three-way split doesn't name but
--     which the same single-leaf's `action` facet-half still needs a
--     home for:
--       - `A_engine_controls[go, action]` -- connect/disconnect +
--         the engine-controls button cluster (`useEngineControls`,
--         `ToolbarEngineCluster.vue`). ACTION only, not one of the
--         ruling's three named INFO vocabularies.
--       - `A_engine_eval[go, info]` -- {winrate, lead}. Grounded in
--         `ToolbarEngineMetrics.vue`'s own `winrateDisplay`/
--         `scoreLeadDisplay` template block (`toolbar.metric.winrate`
--         "WINRATE (W)"/`toolbar.metric.scoreLead` "LEAD",
--         `frontend/src/locales/en.json`) -- the SAME pairing the
--         component's own script groups under one "live engine-
--         evaluation surface" comment.
--       - `A_engine_health[go, info]` -- {pps, latency, watchdog}.
--         Grounded the same file's `metric-pps`/`metric-latency`/
--         watchdog-dot block (`toolbar.metric.pps` "PPS"/
--         `toolbar.metric.latency` "LATENCY"/`toolbar.metric.watchdog`
--         "WATCHDOG") -- three readouts of engine HEALTH/liveness, as
--         distinct from the eval group's board-position judgment.
--       - `A_engine_queue[go, info]` -- {queue}. Grounded in
--         `EngineQueueTooltip.vue`'s own `.queue-metric` badge
--         (`toolbar.metric.queue` "QUEUE").
--
--     WIDTH RESERVATION, DELIBERATELY NOT AUTHORED (disclosed, not
--     silently absorbed -- per this file's own established "measure
--     before reserving" posture, REPAIR PASS/W4 FLOOR CORRECTION/
--     otherColorDebug sections above). Each new leaf's OWN width
--     (`pref 1fr`, `min` omitted -> the loader's own `0px` default,
--     `min`-key.2's own completion rule, SPEC.md §1.1) does NOT cite any
--     per-group pixel floor. A grounded per-group floor IS computable
--     from `ToolbarEngineMetrics.vue`'s own cited `min-width` `ch`
--     values plus the real `en.json` label strings plus
--     `theme.css`'s spacing tokens (the SAME class of derivation
--     `settingsSubstrip`'s own 838px/443px numbers above use) -- summed
--     by hand: eval ~236px (11+6+4+6=27ch x 8px/ch + 2 tight-gaps(4px
--     each) + 1 medium-gap(12px) = 216+8+12), health ~276px
--     (3+4+7+7+8+1(disclosed ESTIMATE, the watchdog dot has no `ch`
--     reservation in the live CSS)=30ch x 8px/ch + 3 tight-gaps(12px) +
--     2 medium-gaps(24px) = 240+12+24), queue ~68px (5+3=8ch x 8px/ch +
--     1 tight-gap(4px) = 64+4) -- but summing these into `min` floors on
--     the new `H(...)`'s own children would raise the SIDE COLUMN's own
--     effective width floor from today's 345px to roughly 580px+gaps
--     (the four groups' own mins would become a hard constraint on the
--     wrapping H's own along-extent, which cross-fills to the column's
--     width), a MAJOR, UNVERIFIED feasibility regression this stage
--     does not introduce unilaterally without a live re-sweep of how
--     the real `.engine-metrics-bar` (a CSS flex row, NOT a fixed
--     four-column grid) actually WRAPS at narrow widths -- the exact
--     same wrapping-row problem `settingsSubstrip`'s own FLOW-CAPABLE
--     SETTINGS SUBSTRIP work item solved with `flow.py`, not yet
--     attempted for this cluster. Filed as a frontier item (this
--     stage's own dispatch report) rather than either inventing an
--     unverified floor or silently leaving the decomposition unstated.
--     Structural decomposition landing now; per-group demand grounding
--     is the honest remaining gap.
--
--     `activity sustained` (which the note above this section states was
--     declared directly on `A_engine`) is RETIRED from this position --
--     `activity` is leaf-only (SPEC.md §16.1) and `A_engine` is no
--     longer a leaf. None of the four new leaves gains `activity`: L15's
--     band-wide clause (b) applies only to DIRECT LEAF children of a
--     Split, and these four sit one level DEEPER (inside the new
--     `H(...)`, not direct children of the side column `V(...)`) -- so
--     no band-wide obligation reaches them. `find_l15_violations`
--     re-verified `[]` against this file after the change (see this
--     stage's own dispatch report).
