--     samples; there is no such gap here -- three widths spanning this
--     class's own tested range all agree exactly). Reservation moves
--     from the carried-forward `80px` to the measured `92px` directly,
--     no margin added on top. The 12px gap between the old
--     carried-forward figure and this measurement is NOT attributed to
--     any specific structural cause in the measurement report -- it
--     notes only that the gap runs the SAME direction
--     (measured-over-declared) as two other leaves' own REPAIR
--     corrections, not a named cause (e.g. a specific extra
--     padding/border line); reported honestly as an unattributed delta
--     rather than a guessed one.
--
--     Witness: `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-measurement-wave.md`,
--     Measurements 1/4/8, an isolated Playwright rig (own DB copy, ports
--     19100-19102, no engine, no forbidden port touched) -- WITNESSED
--     per that report's own per-claim witness-status summary.
--
--   - LYT PRESENCE ARC P1 (2026-08-12, row 2333, mobile/portrait
--     repetition-first disposition; `.claude/dispatch-reports/
--     lyt-p1-presence-model.md`) -- CONTROL-PANEL DEMOTION. The
--     control-panel `T(...)[BLACK BOX]` gains `@demote(h 778px)` --
--     the FIRST composite (Exclusive) presence demotion in either
--     encoding, per a scoped, disclosed loader/presence.py widening
--     (see `loader._load_demote_presence`'s own docstring for why an
--     Exclusive, unlike a Split, is eligible: every T-child already
--     shares one rectangle and only one is ever visible, so the whole
--     group is already ONE presence-relevant unit, the same way a
--     single leaf is).
--
--     THE THRESHOLD, DERIVED FROM ALREADY-NAMED FACTS, NOT A NEW
--     NUMBER (row 2047's own "a decision posed in pixels is a
--     defect" discipline). This row (`H(tree, T(...), previewBoard)`)
--     is nameable-absent below the width at which its own pinned
--     664px floor PLUS its row-sibling `tree`'s own 110px floor PLUS
--     one row gap can no longer both be granted (previewBoard is
--     already absent under the `default`/`demoted` valuations this
--     matrix checks -- a `@toggle(user, release)` slot, default-off --
--     so its own 160px is not part of THIS threshold's own sum; were
--     previewBoard also present, as under `all-present`, the row would
--     need 942px = 664+110+160+2*4, a fact this comment names but the
--     THRESHOLD itself does not encode, since `@demote` measures one
--     constant and `all-present` is this repository's own diagnostic
--     upper envelope, not a feasibility-bearing valuation, per the
--     M2b2b census's own mid-flight framing):
--       664px (T's own pinned floor, M2 STAGE B2a above, itself
--         traced to CP-analysis's own composite floor)
--     + 110px (tree's own floor, W4 FLOOR SOFTENING above,
--         `layout-model.ts`'s TREE_PANEL_MIN_WIDTH_PX)
--     +   4px (one `--space-tight` row gap, this row's own already-
--         declared `gap 4px`, charged once since only 2 children
--         -- tree, T(...) -- remain once previewBoard is pruned)
--     = 778px.
--
--     `coverage_matrix.py`'s own `DEMOTED_EXTRA_WIDGETS` set gains
--     `"BLACK BOX"` (this Exclusive's own `[BLACK BOX]` tag, which
--     now doubles as its presence identity -- see `presence.py`'s own
--     P1 docstring section) for THIS class -- the "demoted" row is a
--     DIAGNOSTIC coverage point (does landscape stay solvable if the
--     control panel also leaves), not a change to landscape's own
--     `default` valuation, per row 2333's own explicit "do NOT shrink
--     any desktop demand to get there." Landscape's `default` valuation
--     is UNCHANGED by this arc -- `boardRail`/`previewBoard`/`A_setup`
--     remain the only three absent-by-default widgets here; the
--     control panel stands by default at every landscape size this
--     repository's own representative-size tables check (all comfortably
--     above 778px).
--
--   - ENGINE-CONTROLS WIDTH FLOOR (2026-08-13, frontier item B2b closed,
--     `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-wB2-controls-menu.md`, wave W-B2's own
--     live measurement). The ENGINE-ROW HEIGHT RE-GROUNDING item above
--     (item (4)) fixed this row's shared HEIGHT (60px -> 80px) against
--     `A_engine_controls`' own measured 3-row need; it left every one of
--     the four groups' own WIDTH at the loader's `0px` default,
--     "DELIBERATELY NOT AUTHORED" per item (1)'s own disclosure above,
--     pending a live per-group measurement pass. That pass has now run
--     for `A_engine_controls` specifically (the other three -- eval/
--     health/queue -- remain UNEXERCISED, unchanged by this item, per
--     that same disclosure's own "per-group demand grounding is the
--     honest remaining gap").
--
--     THE THRESHOLD, ARITHMETIC, NOT A GUESS (row 2047's own "a decision
--     posed in pixels is a defect" discipline still applies to how this
--     number is REACHED, not to whether the sizing bag itself is
--     numeric -- LYT's own `min`/`pref`/`max` triple is inherently px;
--     what row 2047 forbids is presenting or picking among CANDIDATES in
--     px terms, not authoring a derived px fact once a single arithmetic
--     path leads to it). Wave W-B2 live-measured `.engine-controls`' own
--     five buttons at their WORST-CASE label variants (Playwright, real
--     `ToolbarEngineControls.vue`, isolated rig): Mint Card(s) 105.625px,
--     Learn Path 90.015625px, Play 43.21875px, Match/**Stop Match**
--     90.015625px (the wider of the two), Connect/**Disconnect**
--     90.015625px (the wider of the two) -- with `--space-tight` (4px)
--     between buttons and the SAME 24px `.toolbar-btn` row height this
--     file's own item (4) above already measured and reserves. Greedy
--     sequential flex-wrap (CSS Flexbox 9.3's own line-assignment,
--     cross-checked against live-measured row counts at three widths)
--     over those worst-case widths finds the EXACT column width where 4
--     rows (108px+, clipping this row's own 80px reservation) collapses
--     to 3 (80px, exact fit): the last two items' own row,
--     `90.015625 + 4 + 90.015625 = 184.03125px` -- below that column
--     width the cluster needs a 4th row; at or above it, 3 rows suffice.
--     `184.03125px` is therefore the exact width this leaf must never be
--     granted less than for its already-reserved 80px row height to stay
--     honest. `compiler.py` declares INTEGER `(w,h)` CP-SAT variables
--     (SPEC.md 8's own "Decision variables" line) -- a `min 184px`
--     floor would let the solver legally choose exactly 184px, 0.03125px
--     short of the real breakpoint, so the floor is the CEILING of the
--     exact threshold, `185px`, not the truncation the measurement
--     report's own prose citation uses.
--
--     NO MARGIN ADDED ON TOP -- the SAME "exact multi-point-agreeing
--     constant needs no interpolation margin" posture the MEASUREMENT-
--     GROUNDED ENCODING PASS item's own `A_setup` correction above
--     established ("not a single-pinned-size sweep-maximum needing this
--     file's own separate `+~10px margin` posture... there is no such
--     gap here"). `184.03125px` is a closed-form geometric fact (a sum
--     of independently-measured constants), not a sample between which
--     an unmeasured gap could hide -- the file's own margin posture
--     exists for THAT gap specifically, which does not exist here. Only
--     the integer-px rounding above applies.
--
--     WHY PLAIN `min`, NOT `min <axis>`/L12 OR `floor <axis>`/L16 (SPEC.md
--     16, read in full before this edit). `A_engine_controls` is a direct
--     child of the `H(...)` this comment's own row wraps -- an ordinary
--     SPLIT-CHILD position, not the root and not a direct child of an
--     Exclusive/T node. `min <axis>` (L12) is legal ONLY at that
--     both-axes position (`wellformed.find_l12_violations`'s own
--     structural refusal fires everywhere else, `loader._load_axis_mins`'
--     docstring states the same restriction from the load-time side) --
--     illegal here by construction, not merely inadvisable. `floor
--     <axis>` (L16) is LEAF-legal anywhere, but its own trigger (clause
--     (a), `wellformed.find_l16_violations`) is scoped to a leaf that has
--     ALREADY claimed `content unbounded` plus `elastic <axis>` plus
--     `scroll <axis>` -- i.e. a leaf that reasoned about having too MUCH
--     room and needs to also reason about too LITTLE. `A_engine_controls`
--     declares `content bounded` (a fixed five-button vocabulary, never
--     `elastic`, never `scroll`) -- L16's own narrative does not describe
--     this leaf, and (per `find_l16_violations`' own docstring) `floor`
--     is SOLVER-INERT regardless ("compiler.py never reads floor_axes...
--     what is NOT inert is the reservation clause (b) obliges... an
--     ordinary `min`") -- declaring it here would add words the
--     CP-SAT model never reads, not a real floor. The BASE grammar's
--     plain `min <extent>` key, which every Split child already carries
--     for its own along-axis (SPEC.md 4, the un-amended base sizing
--     production) IS the legal, solver-visible construct at this
--     position -- no STOP-and-report needed, since a legal construct
--     genuinely exists; it simply predates Amendment 8 rather than
--     belonging to it.
--
--     FEASIBILITY, RE-SOLVED, NOT ASSUMED. `min 185px` raises this row's
--     own hard floor sum (185 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 3*4px gap = 197px) against
--     the side column's own `min 345px` -- comfortably inside it at every
--     representative point this file's own `coverage_matrix.py` checks
--     (landscape: 1920x1080, 2560x1440, 1280x1024; portrait: all five
--     `PORTRAIT_SIZES`, where this row's own parent is the PORTRAIT
--     ROOT's `V(...)`, cross-filled to the FULL device width -- 420px at
--     the narrowest representative point, 197px well inside it). Re-
--     solved directly (not merely reasoned about): every point OPTIMAL
--     before this edit stays OPTIMAL after; landscape 1280x1024 was
--     ALREADY `INFEASIBLE` before this edit, for the presence-independent
--     board/tree-row collision SPEC.md 11/12 already document (unrelated
--     to the engine row entirely) -- unchanged, not newly caused. The
--     OTHER three groups (eval/health/queue) are UNAFFECTED in either
--     direction: both before and after this edit they solve to `0px` at
--     every representative point, a PRE-EXISTING, disclosed gap in this
--     model's own stage-3 objective (`runner._gather_reach_preferred_
--     widgets` only auto-enrolls plain-`px`-`pref` leaves into the
--     reach-preferred stage -- an `fr`-`pref` leaf like these three has
--     no stage rewarding it for reaching any particular share, so the
--     solver is free to leave it at its own `0px` floor whenever ANY
--     feasible partition exists, which the real CSS Grid realization's
--     OWN `1fr`-track semantics (SPEC.md 10) does NOT reproduce -- CSS
--     Grid genuinely splits `1fr` tracks evenly). This solver/realization
--     divergence PRE-DATES this edit (verified: the three groups already
--     solved to `0px` before `A_engine_controls` gained a floor) and is
--     out of THIS item's own scope to close -- named, not silently
--     inherited.
layout lengyue-landscape =
  {min 0px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 12px} H(
    @toggle(user, release) {min 168px, pref 168px, max 168px} boardRail[common, info+action],
    {pref 1fr} V(
      {pref maximize, aspect 1} B[board],
      {min 24px, pref 24px, max 24px} I_board[board, info],
      {min 28px, pref 28px, max 28px} A_board[board, action]
    ),
    {min 345px, pref 32fr, max 340px+60ch, gap 4px} V(
      {80px, envelope: {disconnected, connected}, gap 4px} H(
        {min 185px, pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_controls[go, action],
        {pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_eval[go, info],
        {pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_health[go, info],
        {pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_queue[go, info]
      ),
      @demote(h 616px) {160px, content bounded, activity occasional} A_app[common, action],
      @toggle(user, release) {92px, content bounded, activity occasional} A_setup[common, action],
      {pref 1fr, gap 4px} H(
        {min 110px, pref 1fr, max inf} tree[board, info+action],
        @demote(h 778px) {min 664px, pref 664px, max 664px} T(
          {min 160px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v, elastic h, floor v 160px, edge v unit, unit v 32px} CP-library[common],
          {min 160px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v, elastic h, floor v 160px, edge v unit, unit v 39px} CP-cards[common],
          {min 443px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
            {77px, boundary, content bounded} settingsSubstrip[common],
            {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf} T(
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content bounded} SP_session[common],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content bounded} SP_analysisEnv[common],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content bounded} SP_cardSets[common],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v, elastic h, floor v 200px, edge v item} SP_advancedRegistry[common],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content bounded} SP_analysis[common],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v, elastic h, floor v 200px, edge v item} SP_keybindings[common]
            )
          ),
          {min 664px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
            {min 80px, pref 80px, max 80px, boundary, content designed} timelineStrip[go],
            {min 160px, pref 1fr, max inf} T(
              {min 160px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
                {min 90px, pref 90px, max 90px, boundary, content designed} AT_basic_interval[go],
                {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_basic_scoreLead[go],
                {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_basic_mergedDelta[go]
              ),
              {min 160px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
                {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_dist_deltaDist[go],
                {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_dist_mistakeGap[go]
              ),
              {min 160px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
                {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_stab_stability[go],
                {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_stab_crossCorr[go]
              ),
              {min 580px, pref 580px, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_multires[go]
            )[ANALYSIS TABS]
          ),
          {min 204px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
            {min 264px, pref 264px, max 264px, boundary, content designed} otherColorDebug[debug],
            {min 160px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v, edge v continuous} otherBand[common]
          )
        )[BLACK BOX],
        @toggle(user, release) {min 160px, pref 160px, max 160px, aspect 1} previewBoard[common, info]
      )
    )
  )
